    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "[MiniTest.expect.reference_screenshot](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-test.html#minitest.expect.reference_screenshot) prints output like this when the screenshot isn't as expected:\n\n```\n  Cause: different `attr` cell at line 4 column 23, reference = \"3\", observed = \"2\"\n  Reference:\n  -|---------|---------|---------|---------|\n  1|left      right                         \n  2|plain background                        \n  3|~                                       \n  4|~                                       \n  5|[No Name] [+]         1,1            All\n  6|                                        \n  \n  -|---------|---------|---------|---------|\n  1|0000111111000000000000000000000000000000\n  2|0000000000000000000000000000000000000000\n  3|2222222222222222222222222222222222222222\n  4|2222222222222222222222333222222222222222\n  5|3333333333333333333333333333333333333333\n  6|4444444444444444444444444444444444444444\n  \n  Observed:\n  -|---------|---------|---------|---------|\n  1|left      right                         \n  2|plain background                        \n  3|~                                       \n  4|~                                       \n  5|[No Name] [+]         1,1            All\n  6|                                        \n  \n  -|---------|---------|---------|---------|\n  1|0000111111000000000000000000000000000000\n  2|0000000000000000000000000000000000000000\n  3|2222222222222222222222222222222222222222\n  4|2222222222222222222222222222222222222222\n  5|3333333333333333333333333333333333333333\n  6|4444444444444444444444444444444444444444\n```\n\nTo make it easier to spot the differences I think it would be nice if differing cells were highlighted with an ANSI invert. Additionally displaying screens side-by-side would help if they're not too wide (but this would probably take a setting to configure the maximum desired width).\n\n<img width=\"1005\" height=\"397\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/81d1c57e-8f36-495a-9731-666f87ad2f69\" />",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nHighlighting the different cell is an interesting and probably a doable idea. Not sure how I feel about *all* different cells: that would require more computations and would be too much in frequent cases of \"shifted\" attribute codes. But maybe highlighting cell in both text and attribute if one of them is different would be useful.\n\nThe side-by-side would also indeed be useful, but doing that would most certainly increase complexity by more than I would have liked.\n\nI'll take a look.",
